    {
      "id": "claim_46b04c6800794d73b09cc3715dfd814d",
      "statement": "The product state machine defines canonical states idle/preparing/ready/playing/paused/buffering/ended/error sourced from Media3 events (onIsPlayingChanged, STATE_BUFFERING, STATE_ENDED, onMediaItemTransition, controller failures); Media3 remains the transport source of truth while the app state machine defines reactions, and a buffering-induced isPlaying flip must not be treated as a user pause.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/architecture/PLAYBACK_STATE_MACHINE.md#L1-L42",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:8c9a70193ecdb8ac9553686a66f11f02f572cefc0b11637173eed8a24bccb8e0:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_7fb1a75cfbd84db5b0b9e7effc84264a",
      "statement": "ControllerPlaybackStateSynchronizer.sync is the single snapshot-to-UI mapping point: it resolves mediaId as a decimal Song.id (non-numeric ids are ignored, keeping the current song), aligns PlayQueue.currentIndex by song id only when the current queue item differs (so duplicate occurrences are not snapped to the first match), accepts durations only as non-negative values from snapshots (C.TIME_UNSET filtered to null upstream), and recomputes same-name versions only when the song actually changed.",
      "evidence": [
