    {
      "id": "claim_f04105f1a20b44a18d084ad847b79544",
      "statement": "Live-session restore applies the snapshot only to the UI queue shadow, currentSong, and sameNameSongs and never touches the controller (no queue rebuild, no restore position, no isPlaying overwrite — real position/state come from the post-connect snapshot sync); full restore (empty controller queue) prepares the controller queue at the restore position without autoplay; in both branches the UI queue must be restored because controller snapshot sync only adjusts currentIndex and never fills songs, and PlaybackController.prepareQueue additionally self-guards against overwriting a live session.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://feature/player/src/main/java/cn/com/dcsgo/mihx/feature/player/PlayerPersistenceFacade.kt#L62-L122",
