    {
      "id": "claim_9dda27d5f941456c9e4df5c708a989c7",
      "statement": "Playback persistence is decoupled from progress ticks: the ticker routes every position write through PlayerPlaybackStateAutosaver which throttles to one save per 5 seconds (syncPlaybackState then savePlaybackState), savePlaybackStateAsync captures the position on the caller thread before moving the DataStore write to IO, save failures are logged but never interrupt playback control, and an empty-session save skips the write while keeping any existing snapshot (protecting against the UI-rebuild window that previously erased valid snapshots); explicit clears go through clearPlaybackState.",
      "evidence": [
        {
